}}

==Enemy==
Ms. Madonna has many knockbacks, short range and an Area Attack with a 100% chance to [[Knockback|knockback]] cats and create a Lv.3 [[Wave Attack]]. This enemy can be dealt with very easily when she's alone, but when supported by heavy hitters such as [[Teacher Bun Bun]] or [[Zang Roo]], she can become quite the nuisance.

==Strategy==
Due to Ms. Madonna's low damage output, the player can use tanky units like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] or [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]], or [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune cats]] like [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]]. Note that due to being knocked back with the first attack, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] will not block the wave attack if it's in Ms. Madonna's range (130 < 200).

You can also use [[:Category:Cats with Knockback Immunity|cats that are immune to knockback]] to prevent the enemies' front line from moving forward. This is especially important in later stages, where there are powerful backliners that could advance. It is best to defeat her as fast as possible as she can become an annoying support for the enemies.

